Immediate guardrail readout:
  C2/BU residue charge present on 20/20 q-rows.
  GW magnitude switch ON on 7/20 q-rows.
  Requested contrast: q=4,7 are ON; q=5,6 are off.
  Therefore a q-uniform topological flag cannot be the magnitude switch.

Quotient guardrail theorem target:
  A quotient may use C2/BU or C6 topology to close a residue/equioscillation
  obligation.  If it claims a q-specific magnitude conclusion, it must retain
  or restore at least one of:
    (1) the HYP-3413 q mod 3 / Eisenstein arithmetic switch;
    (2) the HYP-3417 labelled owner-current packet for local mixed fibers;
    (3) the S259/HYP-3418 two-adic covering-floor descent signal;
    (4) the HYP-3415 decorrelation floor / Rprime inequality.

